  "text": "Nine done. For the last five, a sentence and a line of code apiece. Series map works value by value on one column, from a function or a lookup. Apply works along an axis, a row or a column at a time. Data frame map works on every cell. Method chaining writes the steps top to bottom, query, assign, group, sum, with no throwaway variables in between. For a CASE, use NumPy select, with a list of conditions and a default. Pandas has case when too. Start it from the default, or rows that match nothing keep their old value. The category D type, short for data type, stores each distinct string once, and a small code per row. Three hundred regions drop from eight thousand nine hundred bytes to four hundred eighteen. And for dates, to datetime parses them, the D T accessor, short for datetime, reaches their parts, and resample groups them by time. By week, a hundred eighty, one seventy, and seventy. Nearly all of this translates straight into SQL. Groupby becomes group by, merge becomes a join, and transform becomes a window function. Next: SQL.",
